SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a blend rolling on an edge that reaches a vertex of the edge
where the next edge turns away from the ball goes on as the ball's turn
about that vertex, and a side of a blend reduced to a point becomes a
degenerated edge (mitcad#237, with 0170).

- ChFi3d_Builder::StartSol, where a blend rolling on an edge (the obstacle)
  ends at a vertex: (a) where the blend's contact stayed at the vertex and
  the same edge runs on from it in the walking direction (the ball turned
  about the vertex, or stood while its other contact swept round it), the
  next blend rolls on along that edge from the vertex; (b) where no edge of
  the reference face continues tangentially and the ball's centre at the
  blend's end (ChFi3d_BallCentreAtEnd, the circle of its end section) lies
  behind the new edge's start, the next blend starts at the vertex on the
  old edge, so that the walk turns the ball about the vertex (0170) until
  it can roll on. Before, the next blend started on the new edge, whose
  solutions there do not touch the ball before it.
- ChFi3d_FilDS: the contact curve of a side whose 3d curve is a point (the
  side of a blend turning about a vertex) is nullified like a degenerated
  side, spanning the blend's surface as the other side does: the blend's
  face gets a degenerated edge and the face beyond no edge. Before, it got
  an edge of no length (BRepCheck_InvalidRange, or the corner failed).
